<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Division of errors Q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An athlete runs a measured distance of \({@distance@}\) m in a recorded time of \({@time@}\) s, both correct to the nearest whole unit. Their average speed is calculated by dividing distance by time. Find:</p>

<p>(a)  The absolute error in his speed.</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) The relative error in his speed.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) The percentage error in his speed.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3> Worked Solution.</h3>
<p>The distance was recorded as \({@distance@}\) m and the time as \({@time@}\) s, both correct to the nearest whole unit.</p>

<p><strong>Absolute errors in the individual measurements:</strong></p>
<p>Since each measurement is correct to the nearest whole unit, the absolute error in each is half of the smallest unit (1 unit):</p>
<p>\[ \text{Distance error} = {@distance_err@} \text{ m}, \qquad \text{Time error} = {@time_err@} \text{ s} \]</p>

<p><strong>Important:</strong> When dividing two measured quantities, the <em>maximum</em> possible value of the result comes from pairing the <em>largest</em> possible numerator with the <em>smallest</em> possible denominator (since dividing by a smaller number gives a larger result). So:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Max distance} = {@distance@} + {@distance_err@} = {@max_distance@} \text{ m}, \qquad \text{Min time} = {@time@} - {@time_err@} = {@min_time@} \text{ s} \]</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Absolute error in the speed:</strong></p>
<p>Using the recorded measurements:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Working speed} = \frac{{@distance@}}{{@time@}} = {@W_speed@} \text{ m/s} \]</p>
<p>Using the maximum distance and minimum time:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Maximum speed} = \frac{{@max_distance@}}{{@min_time@}} = {@max_speed@} \text{ m/s} \]</p>
<p>\[ \text{Absolute error} = \text{Maximum speed} - \text{Working speed} = {@max_speed@} - {@W_speed@} = {@ta1@} \text{ m/s} \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Relative error:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Relative error} = \frac{\text{Absolute error}}{\text{Working speed}} = \frac{{@ta1@}}{{@W_speed@}} \approx {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Percentage error:</strong></p>
<p>\[ \text{Percentage error} = \text{Relative error} \times 100\% = {@ta2@} \times 100\% \approx {@ta3@}\% \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
